  "routeAdjustment": "The local search found the native level-one discriminant division and modular norm APIs, but no existing integrality consumer for these original functions. Reuse them directly: weight induction gives exactly the needed coefficient reduction; interpolation of native norms gives an actual orbit relation. This avoids a general graded modular-form ring presentation, elliptic-curve moduli or Puiseux foundations for finite-place exhaustion. Ported proof terms compile under unchanged pins and limits; only the unavailable generic function-coercion additive hom was replaced by its explicit lawful modular-form coercion. Public constructions have documentation and all proof consumers are audited.",
  "discharged": "Every weight 12m level-one modular expansion is Delta^m times a polynomial in the actual j expansion. Native modular norms and finite interpolation construct the coefficients of the actual orbit product as level-one forms. A proved vanishing identity and explicit leading coefficient produce a monic polynomial over C[j] for g/Delta^m at every actual Gamma0 level. Injective subfield transport proves integrality inside the original field when its discriminant-power expansion equals the given modular expansion. That representation remains an explicit narrower hypothesis in this consumer.",
  "remaining": "Deriving the discriminant-power representation from boundedness by removing singularities and clearing all cusp poles, finite-place exhaustion and orbit separation, elliptic ramification and cardinalities, numerical genus, regular-differential cusp-form realization, and period/arithmetic/symmetric-power gates remain required. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
